WEBVTT

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:52.876
The Mutiny on the Bounty Copyright Black Cat Publishing Chapter 1 The Ship It was a cold morning in the winter of 1787.

00:00:52.936 --> 00:00:59.247
Tom Barnes was very excited when he arrived at Spithead.

00:00:59.307 --> 00:01:03.778
Tom wanted to find his ship, the Bounty.

00:01:03.838 --> 00:01:08.359
He stopped an old sailor with a friendly face.

00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:11.810
Excuse me, where's the Bounty?

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:13.540
Tom asked.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.282
The sailor looked at Tom's new uniform and he smiled.

00:01:18.342 --> 00:01:20.034
How old are you?

00:01:20.094 --> 00:01:21.465
He asked him.

00:01:21.525 --> 00:01:23.046
I'm fourteen.

00:01:23.106 --> 00:01:24.798
Replied Tom.

00:01:24.857 --> 00:01:26.458
Come with me.

00:01:26.518 --> 00:01:28.230
The sailor said.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.232
The bounty is over there I think.

00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:36.116
Tom and the sailor walked together towards a large ship.

00:01:36.176 --> 00:01:37.696
Ah yes.

00:01:37.756 --> 00:01:40.348
The sailor said after a while.

00:01:40.408 --> 00:01:42.258
There she is.

00:01:42.318 --> 00:01:44.729
Who is she?

00:01:44.789 --> 00:01:46.630
Tom asked him.

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:50.171
We call all the ships she.

00:01:50.231 --> 00:01:52.002
The sailor explained.

00:01:52.062 --> 00:01:54.413
And you must do the same.

00:01:54.473 --> 00:01:57.564
That's how real sailors talk.

00:01:57.624 --> 00:02:00.716
Soon they arrived at the bounty.

00:02:00.776 --> 00:02:04.628
A sailor saw Tom and saluted politely.

00:02:04.688 --> 00:02:09.964
Tom saluted the sailor back and turned to the old sailor.

00:02:10.023 --> 00:02:12.058
Thank you for your help.

00:02:12.118 --> 00:02:13.608
He said to him.

00:02:13.668 --> 00:02:19.531
He looked up at the bounty for a moment and then turned back to the old sailor.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.221
She's so big.

00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:24.982
The old sailor smiled at him.

00:02:25.042 --> 00:02:27.123
You learn quickly.

00:02:27.183 --> 00:02:28.464
He told him.

00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:31.805
That's one of the two things you must do.

00:02:31.865 --> 00:02:34.866
Learn everything you can.

00:02:34.926 --> 00:02:38.958
And what's the second thing I must do?

00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:40.425
Tom asked him.

00:02:40.485 --> 00:02:41.983
That's easy.

00:02:42.042 --> 00:02:44.094
The old sailor replied.

00:02:44.153 --> 00:02:47.495
Obey your captain.

00:02:47.555 --> 00:02:51.508
The old sailor walked away from Tom.

00:02:51.568 --> 00:02:54.928
Learn and obey.

00:02:54.988 --> 00:02:56.530
Tom thought.

00:02:56.590 --> 00:02:58.930
It's good advice.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.382
Now Tom went inside the bounty.

00:03:02.442 --> 00:03:06.424
He walked on the deck and looked up at the masts.

00:03:06.484 --> 00:03:08.711
They were very tall.

00:03:08.771 --> 00:03:12.490
He knew that all the sailors had to climb them.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.632
For a moment he was afraid.

00:03:15.692 --> 00:03:17.634
But I can learn.

00:03:17.694 --> 00:03:19.635
He decided.

00:03:19.695 --> 00:03:23.298
Then he went down below the deck.

00:03:23.358 --> 00:03:26.130
He wanted to find his cabin.

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:30.014
It was dark and there were a lot of sailors there.

00:03:30.074 --> 00:03:33.946
The sailors were noisy and Tom was frightened of them.

00:03:34.006 --> 00:03:37.756
They were men and he was only a boy.

00:03:37.816 --> 00:03:41.034
Suddenly the sailors were silent.

00:03:41.094 --> 00:03:44.196
They looked at someone behind Tom.

00:03:44.255 --> 00:03:47.988
Tom turned round and saw an officer.

00:03:48.047 --> 00:03:51.130
The officer was a young man.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:56.172
He smiled at the men and then he looked kindly at Tom.

00:03:56.232 --> 00:03:58.494
You must be Tom Barnes.

00:03:58.554 --> 00:04:01.676
He said, I'm Fletcher Christian.

00:04:01.736 --> 00:04:04.908
I can show you the ship if you want.

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:08.920
I've got time before the captain comes aboard.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.510
Yes, please.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.702
Tom agreed.

00:04:11.761 --> 00:04:14.724
I want to know everything about her.

00:04:14.784 --> 00:04:18.196
Mr. Christian laughed.

00:04:18.255 --> 00:04:19.667
That's good.

00:04:19.727 --> 00:04:24.270
He said a young man needs to know his ship well.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.482
His ship and the men in her.

00:04:27.542 --> 00:04:32.036
Mr. Christian and Tom walked around the ship together.

00:04:32.096 --> 00:04:35.790
Mr. Christian showed Tom the ship's cannons.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.754
They stood next to one of the cannons.

00:04:38.814 --> 00:04:45.557
There were two sailors on the other side of the deck, but they did not see the officer and Tom.

00:04:45.617 --> 00:04:48.439
My brother knows Bligh.

00:04:48.498 --> 00:04:53.532
One of the sailors said, but you don't know him, George.

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:57.414
The other sailor said, you don't know the captain.

00:04:57.434 --> 00:05:01.506
He's the worst captain in the Navy.

00:05:01.566 --> 00:05:03.387
The first sailor continued.

00:05:03.447 --> 00:05:05.401
My brother told me.

00:05:05.461 --> 00:05:09.805
Bligh is cruel, and he uses the whip a lot.

00:05:09.825 --> 00:05:11.105
That's enough talk.

00:05:11.165 --> 00:05:14.226
Mr. Christian said loudly to the two sailors.

00:05:14.286 --> 00:05:17.537
Go up on deck and help the other men.

00:05:17.597 --> 00:05:19.177
Yes, sir.

00:05:19.237 --> 00:05:21.348
The sailors replied quickly.

00:05:21.408 --> 00:05:23.158
Brave men, Tom.

00:05:23.218 --> 00:05:24.898
Mr. Christian repeated.

00:05:24.958 --> 00:05:26.469
Brave men.

00:05:26.529 --> 00:05:32.290
And it's our responsibility to keep them happy.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:39.360
Chapter 2 Captain Bligh.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:44.142
Tom was very busy in the next few days.

00:05:44.202 --> 00:05:51.584
The sailors worked hard to prepare the ship for the long voyage, and Tom worked hard too.

00:05:51.643 --> 00:05:56.564
His friend, Mr. Christian, taught him many things.

00:05:56.624 --> 00:06:00.786
One day he showed Tom how to climb the masts.

00:06:00.846 --> 00:06:03.486
Tom was afraid at first.

00:06:03.546 --> 00:06:06.835
Then he climbed up to the top of the mast.

00:06:06.895 --> 00:06:10.714
The port looked very small from up there.

00:06:10.774 --> 00:06:16.177
The young officer also taught Tom about navigation.

00:06:16.236 --> 00:06:19.708
They spent a lot of time together.

00:06:19.768 --> 00:06:24.800
Mr. Christian was kind and Tom liked him.

00:06:24.859 --> 00:06:28.291
Tom watched his friend with the sailors.

00:06:28.351 --> 00:06:33.818
Fletcher Christian told them what to do because that was his job.

00:06:33.878 --> 00:06:38.898
But he was always polite, and the sailors liked him.

00:06:38.958 --> 00:06:41.370
Be good to the men, Tom.

00:06:41.429 --> 00:06:43.211
His friend advised him.

00:06:43.271 --> 00:06:45.543
Sailors are brave men.

00:06:45.603 --> 00:06:48.014
We must treat them well.

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:52.118
Captain Bly came aboard on the third day.

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:55.600
He did not smile when he met the officers.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:07:01.618
He went immediately to his cabin, and he stayed there the whole day.

00:07:01.678 --> 00:07:08.996
Later, Tom heard a conversation between the sailor called George and some other sailors.

00:07:09.056 --> 00:07:11.298
Bloy is back.

00:07:11.358 --> 00:07:12.930
George said.

00:07:12.989 --> 00:07:16.732
He doesn't look very happy to see us.

00:07:16.792 --> 00:07:18.794
I know him.

00:07:18.854 --> 00:07:20.404
Be careful of him.

00:07:20.424 --> 00:07:23.317
He's a terror.

00:07:23.377 --> 00:07:25.539
What's the captain like?

00:07:25.599 --> 00:07:28.091
Tom asked Fletcher Christian.

00:07:28.151 --> 00:07:33.585
One of the sailors said that Captain Bligh is one of the best officers in the Navy.

00:07:33.645 --> 00:07:34.976
Fletcher told him.

00:07:35.036 --> 00:07:36.737
I know him well.

00:07:36.797 --> 00:07:38.489
He looked at Tom.

00:07:38.548 --> 00:07:42.862
Sometimes the sailors don't understand their officers, Tom.

00:07:42.882 --> 00:07:47.766
A captain's job is a difficult one, you know?

00:07:47.826 --> 00:07:53.102
That evening, Tom ate with all the officers in the captain's cabin.

00:07:53.162 --> 00:07:58.066
There was a long table and Captain Bly sat at one end.

00:07:58.126 --> 00:08:01.417
Come and sit with me, Mr. Barnes.

00:08:01.477 --> 00:08:03.427
Captain Bly said.

00:08:03.487 --> 00:08:07.958
The youngest officer always sits with the captain.

00:08:08.018 --> 00:08:09.499
He explained.

00:08:09.559 --> 00:08:11.489
Tom sat down.

00:08:11.549 --> 00:08:14.840
He did not know what to say to the captain.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:17.391
Is this your first voyage?

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.711
Captain Bly asked him.

00:08:19.771 --> 00:08:23.726
Yes, Tom replied nervously.

00:08:23.786 --> 00:08:26.472
Captain Bly smiled at him.

00:08:26.532 --> 00:08:29.344
You have a lot to learn, my boy.

00:08:29.404 --> 00:08:31.126
The captain told him.

00:08:31.186 --> 00:08:34.128
You must ask me lots of questions.

00:08:34.188 --> 00:08:35.509
Thank you, sir.

00:08:35.569 --> 00:08:37.330
Tom said.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:41.323
Now Captain Bly turned to the other officers.

00:08:41.384 --> 00:08:44.856
He asked them about the ship and the sailors.

00:08:44.916 --> 00:08:47.508
Is everything ready for tomorrow?

00:08:47.568 --> 00:08:48.790
He asked.

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:50.171
Yes, sir.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:51.970
The officers told him.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.058
Very good.

00:08:53.118 --> 00:08:54.068
He said.

00:08:54.128 --> 00:08:55.720
He stood up.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.001
Sleep well, gentlemen.

00:08:58.061 --> 00:09:00.623
We leave early in the morning.

00:09:00.683 --> 00:09:03.605
The officers left the captain's cabin.

00:09:03.665 --> 00:09:07.018
What do you think of Captain Bligh now?

00:09:07.078 --> 00:09:09.630
Fletcher Christian asked Tom.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.901
I think he's a good captain.

00:09:11.961 --> 00:09:13.282
Tom answered.

00:09:13.342 --> 00:09:18.056
He's not a terror at all.

00:09:18.116 --> 00:09:22.826
Listening activity.

00:09:22.886 --> 00:09:30.378
Dear mum, I hope you're all well and not missing me too much.

00:09:30.438 --> 00:09:36.990
The ship is very big, but I can find my way around now.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:43.093
I'm learning a lot, but I have to get up very early.

00:09:43.153 --> 00:09:53.668
I met some sailors on the first day I arrived, and the officer I work with is very friendly.

00:09:53.728 --> 00:09:59.912
Today, I learned how to calculate the position of the ship.

00:09:59.972 --> 00:10:05.586
It's difficult, but I think I understand it now.

00:10:05.646 --> 00:10:11.890
The officer I work with is called Fletcher Christian.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:20.586
He also showed me how to climb masts, and today I climbed right to the top.

00:10:20.647 --> 00:10:23.545
It was amazing.

00:10:23.605 --> 00:10:28.813
Yesterday, I sat next to Captain Bligh.

00:10:28.873 --> 00:10:31.534
He's a good captain.

00:10:31.594 --> 00:10:34.964
He's very famous in the Navy.

00:10:35.024 --> 00:10:39.675
The other sailors say, he's a terror.

00:10:39.735 --> 00:10:43.336
But I'm sure he's not that bad.

00:10:43.396 --> 00:10:47.257
He's kind to me, so don't worry.

00:10:47.277 --> 00:10:52.309
I think I'm going to enjoy my voyage.

00:10:52.369 --> 00:10:57.802
I'll be able to send this letter at the next port.

00:10:57.862 --> 00:11:02.404
Give my love to Charlotte and Jane.

00:11:02.464 --> 00:11:05.094
Don't worry about me.

00:11:05.154 --> 00:11:09.166
I'm happy with my new life on board the ship.

00:11:09.226 --> 00:11:13.568
And I'm sure everything will be fine.

00:11:13.627 --> 00:11:18.569
I'll bring you all some presents when I return.

00:11:18.629 --> 00:11:23.028
Love, Tom.

00:11:23.088 --> 00:11:40.670
Chapter 3 The Voyage Begins It was the 23rd of December 1787 when the bounty left Britain, and the ship quickly left land far behind.

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:43.680
The days passed quickly for Tom.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:46.491
He climbed the masts easily now.

00:11:46.551 --> 00:11:54.430
He was not afraid of Captain Bligh anymore, and he sat next to the captain every evening at dinner.

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:57.960
Learn your navigation, Mr. Barnes.

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:00.362
The captain told him one evening.

00:12:00.422 --> 00:12:03.486
It's the most important thing for an officer.

00:12:03.546 --> 00:12:07.500
You must always know the position of the ship.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:13.776
One day, Tom and Fletcher Christian were next to Captain Bligh on the deck.

00:12:13.836 --> 00:12:17.200
The captain had his sextant in his hand.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.234
He explained to Tom how to use it.

00:12:20.294 --> 00:12:23.217
We want to know our position.

00:12:23.277 --> 00:12:27.988
He said, I can find out with this sextant.

00:12:28.048 --> 00:12:31.089
First, I must find the sun.

00:12:31.149 --> 00:12:34.110
He pointed the instrument at the sun.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:37.851
Then he wrote some numbers on a piece of paper.

00:12:37.911 --> 00:12:39.421
Now it's your turn.

00:12:39.481 --> 00:12:41.172
He said to Tom.

00:12:41.232 --> 00:12:45.163
Tom took the sextant and pointed it at the sun.

00:12:45.223 --> 00:12:49.508
Then he too wrote some numbers on a piece of paper.

00:12:49.568 --> 00:12:51.731
Where are we, Mr. Barnes?

00:12:51.791 --> 00:12:54.032
Captain Bligh asked him.

00:12:54.092 --> 00:12:57.642
Tom showed the Captain his piece of paper.

00:12:57.702 --> 00:13:00.433
The Captain studied it for a moment.

00:13:00.493 --> 00:13:02.673
His face was serious.

00:13:02.733 --> 00:13:04.904
This is no good?

00:13:04.964 --> 00:13:06.674
He shouted angrily.

00:13:06.734 --> 00:13:09.044
You must do better than this.

00:13:09.104 --> 00:13:11.855
Then he turned to Fletcher Christian.

00:13:11.915 --> 00:13:15.345
This boy can't use the sextant properly.

00:13:15.405 --> 00:13:16.466
He said.

00:13:16.526 --> 00:13:18.746
Teach him, Mr. Christian.

00:13:18.806 --> 00:13:21.498
Is your responsibility?

00:13:21.558 --> 00:13:25.550
Captain Bly moved away from Tom and Fletcher.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.171
Tom was very unhappy.

00:13:28.230 --> 00:13:29.752
Don't worry.

00:13:29.812 --> 00:13:31.252
Fletcher told him.

00:13:31.312 --> 00:13:33.933
We can practice later today.

00:13:33.993 --> 00:13:38.595
Captain Bly did not talk to Tom for the rest of the day.

00:13:38.655 --> 00:13:42.406
He still looked angry when they met at dinner.

00:13:42.466 --> 00:13:44.578
He is a terror.

00:13:44.637 --> 00:13:46.165
Tom thought.

00:13:46.225 --> 00:13:51.096
A few days later, Tom was on deck with the captain again.

00:13:51.156 --> 00:13:53.126
Well, Mr. Barnes.

00:13:53.186 --> 00:13:57.330
Captain Bly said, Are you ready for some navigation?

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:58.601
Yes, sir.

00:13:58.661 --> 00:14:00.202
Tom answered.

00:14:00.262 --> 00:14:02.844
This time Tom was lucky.

00:14:02.904 --> 00:14:07.838
He wrote the numbers down and gave the piece of paper to the captain.

00:14:07.898 --> 00:14:11.610
Captain Bly studied the numbers silently.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:13.894
Then he smiled at Tom.

00:14:13.954 --> 00:14:15.696
Well done, the boy.

00:14:15.756 --> 00:14:16.686
He said.

00:14:16.746 --> 00:14:19.257
Your calculation is correct.

00:14:19.318 --> 00:14:21.509
It's a good piece of work.

00:14:21.569 --> 00:14:27.712
Tom was very pleased, and his friend Fletcher was happy for him as well.

00:14:27.772 --> 00:14:31.724
That evening, Captain Bly was very cheerful.

00:14:31.784 --> 00:14:37.387
He told Tom stories about fights between enemy ships and adventures.

00:14:37.448 --> 00:14:41.652
He talked about beautiful islands in the Pacific Ocean.

00:14:41.712 --> 00:14:44.526
They are wonderful places, my boy.

00:14:44.546 --> 00:14:45.746
He said.

00:14:45.806 --> 00:14:47.728
The people are friendly.

00:14:47.788 --> 00:14:50.749
The sun shines all day.

00:14:50.809 --> 00:14:54.300
And there is always fruit on the trees.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:59.032
That night, Captain Bly asked Tom to wait in the cabin.

00:14:59.092 --> 00:15:02.684
I want to show you my collection, Mr Barnes.

00:15:02.744 --> 00:15:04.716
The captain told him.

00:15:04.776 --> 00:15:07.846
He took Tom to the back of the cabin.

00:15:07.906 --> 00:15:10.603
There were hundreds of plants there.

00:15:10.663 --> 00:15:13.860
They come from all over the world.

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:16.282
Captain Bly told him proudly.

00:15:16.342 --> 00:15:17.814
They're my hobby.

00:15:17.874 --> 00:15:21.536
He pointed to a large plant with blue flowers.

00:15:21.596 --> 00:15:23.808
This is my favorite.

00:15:23.868 --> 00:15:24.828
He said.

00:15:24.888 --> 00:15:28.112
It comes from a little island in the Pacific.

00:15:28.172 --> 00:15:31.294
It's more than ten years old.

00:15:31.354 --> 00:15:34.897
The captain's not so bad really.

00:15:34.956 --> 00:15:36.158
Tom thought.

00:15:36.218 --> 00:15:38.460
He gets angry sometimes.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:41.576
That's all.

00:15:41.636 --> 00:15:48.047
listening activity.

00:15:48.067 --> 00:15:54.914
Go two squares south-west.

00:15:54.934 --> 00:16:01.080
Now follow on two squares to the west.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:08.288
Turn south-east for four squares.

00:16:08.348 --> 00:16:14.704
Go north again for one square.

00:16:14.764 --> 00:16:26.430
Now turn north east for two squares and north for one square.

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:35.319
This is the position of the ship.

00:16:35.379 --> 00:16:44.956
One day Fletcher and Tom were in Fletcher's cabin together.

00:16:45.017 --> 00:16:48.508
Fletcher took a map out of the desk.

00:16:48.568 --> 00:16:50.919
Come and look at this, Tom.

00:16:50.979 --> 00:16:52.079
He said.

00:16:52.139 --> 00:16:54.880
Tom sat next to his friend.

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:57.141
We're going here.

00:16:57.201 --> 00:16:58.962
Fletcher explained.

00:16:59.022 --> 00:17:02.382
He pointed to a little island in the sea.

00:17:02.442 --> 00:17:05.024
This is Tahiti.

00:17:05.084 --> 00:17:09.520
It's one of the most beautiful islands in the world.

00:17:09.580 --> 00:17:13.896
we're going there to collect breadfruit plants.

00:17:13.956 --> 00:17:18.938
Then we're going to take them all the way to the West Indies.

00:17:18.998 --> 00:17:21.568
That's our mission.

00:17:21.628 --> 00:17:24.259
What's Tahiti like?

00:17:24.319 --> 00:17:26.290
Tom wanted to know.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.751
It's a beautiful island.

00:17:28.811 --> 00:17:36.661
Sailors are always happy to stop there, and the people of Tahiti are very friendly.

00:17:36.721 --> 00:17:40.221
Just then they heard Captain Bligh's voice.

00:17:40.282 --> 00:17:42.644
He was on the deck above them.

00:17:42.704 --> 00:17:45.566
He was angry with one of the sailors.

00:17:45.625 --> 00:17:48.288
That water is for the plants.

00:17:48.348 --> 00:17:49.528
He shouted.

00:17:49.588 --> 00:17:53.071
It isn't for you to drink.

00:17:53.131 --> 00:17:55.293
I'm sorry, sir.

00:17:55.353 --> 00:17:57.724
The sailor said nervously.

00:17:57.784 --> 00:18:00.781
Tom recognized the sailor's voice.

00:18:00.841 --> 00:18:02.426
It was George.

00:18:02.486 --> 00:18:04.347
Mr. Christian.

00:18:04.408 --> 00:18:06.339
Captain Bligh shouted.

00:18:06.399 --> 00:18:08.541
Come onto the deck, please.

00:18:08.601 --> 00:18:10.913
Fletcher ran out of the cabin.

00:18:10.973 --> 00:18:13.875
He went on deck and Tom followed him.

00:18:13.935 --> 00:18:15.957
Arrest that man.

00:18:16.017 --> 00:18:18.028
Captain Bligh ordered.

00:18:18.088 --> 00:18:20.920
Fletcher called two of the sailors.

00:18:20.981 --> 00:18:24.083
Take this man to the captain's cabin.

00:18:24.143 --> 00:18:25.481
He told them.

00:18:25.541 --> 00:18:28.840
The sailors tied George's hands together.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:32.151
Then they took him down to the captain's cabin.

00:18:32.211 --> 00:18:34.922
Captain Bligh was still angry.

00:18:34.982 --> 00:18:37.984
He turned to speak to Fletcher Christian.

00:18:38.044 --> 00:18:40.996
I want discipline on this ship.

00:18:41.056 --> 00:18:42.266
He told him.

00:18:42.326 --> 00:18:46.178
And it's your job to control the sailors.

00:18:46.239 --> 00:18:50.090
Fletcher did not reply to the angry words.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:53.132
We must punish that sailor.

00:18:53.192 --> 00:18:54.709
The captain said.

00:18:54.769 --> 00:18:58.316
You know what to do, Mr. Christian.

00:18:58.376 --> 00:19:02.307
Fletcher Christian did not want to punish the sailor.

00:19:02.367 --> 00:19:04.888
He tried to argue with the captain.

00:19:04.948 --> 00:19:07.929
There's a lot of water on the ship, sir.

00:19:07.989 --> 00:19:08.879
He said.

00:19:08.939 --> 00:19:11.880
The sailor doesn't deserve punishment.

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.491
Punish him, Mr. Christian.

00:19:14.551 --> 00:19:16.412
The captain said.

00:19:16.472 --> 00:19:18.112
Yes, sir.

00:19:18.172 --> 00:19:20.793
Fletcher said unhappily.

00:19:20.853 --> 00:19:26.525
That afternoon all the officers stood on the deck around Captain Bligh.

00:19:26.585 --> 00:19:30.016
Two sailors brought George onto the deck.

00:19:30.077 --> 00:19:32.888
They tied him to one of the masts.

00:19:32.948 --> 00:19:35.949
Then another sailor stepped forward.

00:19:36.009 --> 00:19:42.012
He had a cruel whip, a catter nine tails, in his hand.

00:19:42.072 --> 00:19:47.754
You must whip him twenty times as his punishment.

00:19:47.814 --> 00:19:50.660
Captain Bligh told the sailor.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:52.545
Very good sir."

00:19:52.605 --> 00:19:54.496
The sailor replied.

00:19:54.556 --> 00:19:59.890
He raised the cationine tails, then he hit George on the back.

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:02.731
George cried out.

00:20:02.792 --> 00:20:05.784
But he continued to hit him.

00:20:05.844 --> 00:20:08.315
Tom watched the punishment.

00:20:08.375 --> 00:20:11.567
He was frightened when he saw blood on the deck.

00:20:11.627 --> 00:20:13.538
He closed his eyes.

00:20:13.598 --> 00:20:16.448
He did not want to look anymore.

00:20:16.508 --> 00:20:18.487
It's all right, Tom.

00:20:18.547 --> 00:20:19.998
Fletcher told him.

00:20:20.058 --> 00:20:22.758
The punishment is nearly finished.

00:20:22.818 --> 00:20:28.659
Captain Bligh countered as the sailor hit George.

00:20:28.719 --> 00:20:30.049
19?

00:20:30.069 --> 00:20:30.960
20?

00:20:31.019 --> 00:20:33.200
He called out.

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:35.840
Now take him away.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.691
Some sailors ran forward.

00:20:38.751 --> 00:20:41.521
They untied George from the mast.

00:20:41.581 --> 00:20:48.269
He could not walk, so the sailors carried him away.

00:20:48.329 --> 00:20:59.329
Chapter 5 An Unhappy Ship The sailors were not happy after George's punishment.

00:20:59.390 --> 00:21:04.372
They still did their work, but they looked angrily at the captain.

00:21:04.432 --> 00:21:07.073
Tom was not happy either.

00:21:07.133 --> 00:21:09.804
He talked to Fletcher Christian.

00:21:09.865 --> 00:21:12.946
Captain lies a cruel man.

00:21:13.006 --> 00:21:14.596
He told his friend.

00:21:14.656 --> 00:21:16.397
Don't talk like that.

00:21:16.457 --> 00:21:17.808
Fletcher told him.

00:21:17.868 --> 00:21:21.041
He's our captain, and we must obey him.

00:21:21.101 --> 00:21:24.884
Tom remembered the advice of the old sailor.

00:21:24.944 --> 00:21:28.505
Obey your captain.

00:21:28.565 --> 00:21:33.196
Soon after, there was a terrible storm at sea.

00:21:33.256 --> 00:21:38.288
The wind was very strong and the waves came onto the ship.

00:21:38.348 --> 00:21:40.628
It was cold and wet.

00:21:40.688 --> 00:21:45.440
The crew of the bounty fought the storm for 30 days and nights.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:49.790
Nobody could sleep and there was no hot food.

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:55.679
The sailors worked hard to save the ship, and everyone was exhausted.

00:21:55.739 --> 00:22:00.810
We're all going to die, thought Tom.

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:05.342
One day there was a terrible accident.

00:22:05.402 --> 00:22:09.943
Captain Bligh ordered some sailors to climb the masts.

00:22:10.003 --> 00:22:15.184
It was difficult and dangerous, and they climbed slowly in the wind.

00:22:15.244 --> 00:22:19.510
Suddenly, one of the sailors fell from the mast.

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:22.006
He was very badly hurt.

00:22:22.066 --> 00:22:26.398
The doctor tried to help him, but he died.

00:22:26.458 --> 00:22:30.462
Tom saw George and his friend together.

00:22:30.522 --> 00:22:33.234
Bloys a bad captain.

00:22:33.294 --> 00:22:35.086
George said angrily.

00:22:35.146 --> 00:22:36.997
He doesn't care about the men.

00:22:37.017 --> 00:22:40.450
He's a hard man, George.

00:22:40.510 --> 00:22:43.882
His friend replied, we all know that.

00:22:43.942 --> 00:22:45.963
But what can we do?

00:22:46.024 --> 00:22:47.938
He's the captain.

00:22:47.999 --> 00:22:50.143
I know what we can do.

00:22:50.203 --> 00:22:51.703
George said.

00:22:51.763 --> 00:22:55.805
He took out his knife and showed it to his friend.

00:22:55.865 --> 00:22:57.275
Put that away.

00:22:57.335 --> 00:22:59.056
His friend said quickly.

00:22:59.116 --> 00:23:01.487
You mustn't talk like that.

00:23:01.547 --> 00:23:07.029
At last, the storm passed and the weather was calm again.

00:23:07.089 --> 00:23:10.440
The bounty sailed towards Tahiti.

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:17.908
Tom thought the ship's problems were over, but the good weather brought new difficulties.

00:23:17.968 --> 00:23:24.358
One evening at dinner, Fletcher Christian talked seriously to the captain.

00:23:24.418 --> 00:23:27.572
There's a problem with the water, sir.

00:23:27.632 --> 00:23:28.822
He said.

00:23:28.883 --> 00:23:33.396
Some of the barrels are broken because of the storm.

00:23:33.456 --> 00:23:37.290
Do we have enough water to reach Tahiti?

00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:39.094
The captain asked.

00:23:39.154 --> 00:23:41.206
We can reach Tahiti.

00:23:41.266 --> 00:23:42.576
Fletcher told him.

00:23:42.636 --> 00:23:45.998
But we must give the sailors all the water.

00:23:46.058 --> 00:23:50.060
We can't give water to the plants, sir.

00:23:50.120 --> 00:23:50.930
No.

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:53.191
Shouted Captain Bly angrily.

00:23:53.251 --> 00:23:55.412
The plants are important.

00:23:55.472 --> 00:23:58.488
The crew must drink less water.

00:23:58.548 --> 00:24:02.436
Two cups a day for each sailor, Mr. Christian.

00:24:02.496 --> 00:24:04.208
Two cups a day?

00:24:04.268 --> 00:24:06.079
It's not enough, sir.

00:24:06.139 --> 00:24:07.310
Fletcher said.

00:24:07.370 --> 00:24:11.204
The men need more than two cups a day to survive.

00:24:11.264 --> 00:24:13.746
Give the order, Mr. Christian.

00:24:13.806 --> 00:24:15.597
Captain Bligh replied.

00:24:15.657 --> 00:24:18.010
Two cups a day.

00:24:18.070 --> 00:24:23.024
The next day, Fletcher Christian explained the order to the sailors.

00:24:23.084 --> 00:24:25.077
They were not happy.

00:24:25.138 --> 00:24:28.061
Two caps a day, sir.

00:24:28.121 --> 00:24:29.971
One of them asked.

00:24:30.032 --> 00:24:33.093
We can't work without water.

00:24:33.153 --> 00:24:35.164
It's not right.

00:24:35.224 --> 00:24:38.235
What about the captain's plants, sir?

00:24:38.295 --> 00:24:40.666
Another sailor wanted to know.

00:24:40.726 --> 00:24:42.936
Do we still give them water?

00:24:42.996 --> 00:24:46.098
The plants get their water.

00:24:46.158 --> 00:24:47.638
Fletcher told them.

00:24:47.698 --> 00:24:50.349
We're more important than plants.

00:24:50.409 --> 00:24:52.870
A sailor said angrily.

00:24:52.930 --> 00:24:56.001
Fletcher looked sadly at the men.

00:24:56.062 --> 00:24:58.213
He agreed with them.

00:24:58.274 --> 00:25:00.856
Captain's orders, men.

00:25:00.916 --> 00:25:04.198
He said.

00:25:04.258 --> 00:25:09.111
Listening activity.

00:25:09.171 --> 00:25:12.294
This is Island Radio.

00:25:12.354 --> 00:25:18.948
Well, we've got plenty of music for you today on Island Radio, but first Jane Venders with the weather.

00:25:19.008 --> 00:25:20.518
Good morning!

00:25:20.578 --> 00:25:27.409
Now the weather isn't looking too bad for the next 24 hours and the temperatures are high for this time of year.

00:25:27.469 --> 00:25:31.750
But it will depend on where you are on the island today.

00:25:31.810 --> 00:25:38.932
The north of the island will be mostly clear and sunny all day, with clear skies until midnight.

00:25:38.992 --> 00:25:47.495
In the east there will be a mixture of sunshine and outbreaks of rain in the morning, but becoming sunnier in the afternoon.

00:25:47.555 --> 00:25:53.392
The west of the island will have the worst of the rain with heavy rain until midday.

00:25:53.452 --> 00:26:00.076
There will be some sun in the afternoon and late evening, but it will continue to be cloudy.

00:26:00.136 --> 00:26:09.054
In the south, the weather will be cloudy in the morning, but sunny at later in the afternoon, with strong winds near the coast.

00:26:09.114 --> 00:26:15.698
That's all from me until tomorrow and now back to Mike.

00:26:15.758 --> 00:26:26.061
Chapter 6 Tahiti It was very hot on the ship.

00:26:26.121 --> 00:26:31.704
There were no clouds in the sky and the sun shone all day.

00:26:31.764 --> 00:26:37.186
The sailors worked hard and they were always thirsty.

00:26:37.246 --> 00:26:40.458
They wanted more water.

00:26:40.519 --> 00:26:44.680
Captain Bly was always angry now.

00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:51.972
He did not talk to Tom in his cabin, and very often he shouted at Fletcher Christian.

00:26:52.032 --> 00:26:56.724
The officers were extremely unhappy.

00:26:56.784 --> 00:27:07.486
At last, on the 26th of October, 1788, the bounty reached the island of Tahiti.

00:27:07.547 --> 00:27:10.007
Tom was excited.

00:27:10.067 --> 00:27:12.900
He saw trees on the island.

00:27:12.961 --> 00:27:16.544
Soon there were a lot of canoes in the sea.

00:27:16.604 --> 00:27:21.594
The people of Tahiti came across the sea to welcome the sailors.

00:27:21.654 --> 00:27:26.775
They brought fruit and flowers with them and gave them to the sailors.

00:27:26.835 --> 00:27:30.066
The ship anchored near the island.

00:27:30.126 --> 00:27:32.916
Everything will be all right now.

00:27:32.976 --> 00:27:35.127
George said to his friend.

00:27:35.187 --> 00:27:38.467
Tahiti is the best place in the world.

00:27:38.527 --> 00:27:42.730
The sailors looked at the island and smiled happily.

00:27:42.790 --> 00:27:47.904
Some of them knew the island well, and they told their friends about it.

00:27:47.964 --> 00:27:51.487
It's wonderful, one of them explained.

00:27:51.547 --> 00:28:00.014
The people like sailors, we can eat and drink good things here, and the people are friendly.

00:28:00.074 --> 00:28:04.066
Fletcher Christian went to talk to the captain.

00:28:04.126 --> 00:28:06.438
The men like to eat he?

00:28:06.498 --> 00:28:08.460
He said to captain Bly.

00:28:08.520 --> 00:28:11.329
They want to go on to the island.

00:28:11.389 --> 00:28:14.248
Can I give permission, sir?

00:28:14.308 --> 00:28:18.070
No one can go onto the island yet.

00:28:18.130 --> 00:28:20.142
Captain Bly replied.

00:28:20.202 --> 00:28:23.524
We have work to do, Mr. Christian.

00:28:23.584 --> 00:28:26.314
The sailors are tired, sir.

00:28:26.375 --> 00:28:27.736
Fletcher said.

00:28:27.796 --> 00:28:30.999
They need rest and good food.

00:28:31.059 --> 00:28:33.842
Can't they go there for a few days?

00:28:33.902 --> 00:28:36.603
Didn't you hear me, Mr. Christian?

00:28:36.663 --> 00:28:39.114
Captain Bligh asked angrily.

00:28:39.174 --> 00:28:43.765
No one will go to the island without my permission.

00:28:43.825 --> 00:28:48.267
Tom heard Captain Bligh's angry words to his friend.

00:28:48.327 --> 00:28:50.827
He was sorry for Fletcher.

00:28:50.888 --> 00:28:55.189
Just then, some sailors came to Tom and Fletcher.

00:28:55.249 --> 00:28:57.910
When can we go to the island, sir?

00:28:57.970 --> 00:29:00.525
One of the sailors asked Fletcher.

00:29:00.585 --> 00:29:02.700
I know the island well.

00:29:02.760 --> 00:29:05.021
I've got friends here.

00:29:05.081 --> 00:29:06.992
I'm sorry, men."

00:29:07.052 --> 00:29:08.432
Fletcher replied.

00:29:08.492 --> 00:29:10.694
No one can go yet.

00:29:10.754 --> 00:29:12.704
Captain's orders.

00:29:12.764 --> 00:29:15.176
The men were angry.

00:29:15.236 --> 00:29:18.297
But we always visit the island.

00:29:18.357 --> 00:29:19.878
One of them argued.

00:29:19.938 --> 00:29:21.708
It's not right.

00:29:21.769 --> 00:29:25.760
Captain Bly was soon busy with the islanders.

00:29:25.820 --> 00:29:29.298
He wanted to buy lots of breadfruit plants.

00:29:29.358 --> 00:29:34.765
The islanders brought lots of the plants and the sailors carried them onto the ship.

00:29:34.825 --> 00:29:36.846
More plants?

00:29:36.906 --> 00:29:39.616
George said to his friend.

00:29:39.676 --> 00:29:44.098
One day, Captain Bly decided to go ashore.

00:29:44.158 --> 00:29:47.020
He wanted Tom to go with him.

00:29:47.080 --> 00:29:50.731
They took one of the bounties' little boats.

00:29:50.791 --> 00:29:55.103
A group of islanders met them when they came ashore.

00:29:55.163 --> 00:29:58.020
The islanders gave them presents.

00:29:58.080 --> 00:30:02.430
Then they showed the captain and Tom around the island.

00:30:02.490 --> 00:30:06.814
Tom thought that Tahiti was very beautiful.

00:30:06.874 --> 00:30:10.446
Even Captain Bly seemed happy.

00:30:10.506 --> 00:30:13.438
This is my favorite place.

00:30:13.499 --> 00:30:15.410
He told Tom.

00:30:15.470 --> 00:30:19.192
Tom thought about the sailors on the ship.

00:30:19.252 --> 00:30:22.522
They wanted to come to the island too.

00:30:22.582 --> 00:30:25.241
The men like the island, too.

00:30:25.301 --> 00:30:28.423
He said, they want to come here, sir.

00:30:28.482 --> 00:30:30.283
Captain lie left.

00:30:30.343 --> 00:30:32.644
Ha, ha, don't worry about them.

00:30:32.704 --> 00:30:34.015
He told Tom.

00:30:34.075 --> 00:30:36.196
They can come here soon.

00:30:36.256 --> 00:30:39.117
But first, they must work.

00:30:39.178 --> 00:30:41.408
Discipline, Mr. Barnes.

00:30:41.468 --> 00:30:43.009
Discipline.

00:30:43.069 --> 00:30:45.340
The captain's all right.

00:30:45.400 --> 00:30:46.661
Tom thought.

00:30:46.721 --> 00:30:50.994
He's not a terror, after all.

00:30:51.054 --> 00:30:59.978
Chapter 7 Trouble in Tahiti Weeks passed.

00:31:00.038 --> 00:31:06.160
The bounty had lots of breadfruit plants now, and Captain Bly was happy.

00:31:06.220 --> 00:31:09.641
One day he called Fletcher Christian.

00:31:09.701 --> 00:31:13.072
The sailors couldn't go to the island now.

00:31:13.132 --> 00:31:14.793
He told Fletcher.

00:31:14.853 --> 00:31:16.183
Thank you, sir.

00:31:16.243 --> 00:31:17.874
Fletcher said.

00:31:17.934 --> 00:31:22.310
He went to the sailors and told them the good news.

00:31:22.370 --> 00:31:27.076
Soon Tom saw the banties' little boats in the water.

00:31:27.136 --> 00:31:32.077
They were full of sailors carrying presents for the islanders.

00:31:32.137 --> 00:31:38.739
The sailors went to the island every day now and they made friends with the islanders.

00:31:38.799 --> 00:31:41.179
They ate good food.

00:31:41.239 --> 00:31:46.310
The islanders liked the sailors and they played music for them.

00:31:46.370 --> 00:31:50.942
Some of the sailors fell in love with girls on the island.

00:31:51.002 --> 00:31:53.064
The months passed.

00:31:53.125 --> 00:31:56.028
and the bounty stayed in Tahiti.

00:31:56.088 --> 00:31:58.309
We can't leave yet.

00:31:58.369 --> 00:32:00.560
Fletcher explained to Tom.

00:32:00.620 --> 00:32:03.291
We must wait for the right wind.

00:32:03.351 --> 00:32:06.172
The sailors were happy to wait.

00:32:06.232 --> 00:32:10.254
Some of them spent all their time on the island now.

00:32:10.314 --> 00:32:13.446
They did not return to the ship.

00:32:13.506 --> 00:32:17.877
One day three sailors decided to escape.

00:32:17.937 --> 00:32:20.981
They wanted to live on the island.

00:32:21.042 --> 00:32:25.046
They took one of the ship's boats and some guns.

00:32:25.106 --> 00:32:29.787
Captain Bligh was furious and wanted to punish them.

00:32:29.847 --> 00:32:33.738
He ordered Fletcher Christian to find them.

00:32:33.798 --> 00:32:38.928
Fletcher Christian and Tom went to the island together.

00:32:38.988 --> 00:32:41.419
We must find them, Tom.

00:32:41.479 --> 00:32:43.920
Fletcher said sadly.

00:32:43.980 --> 00:32:51.688
Fletcher and Tom found the three sailors on the island and brought them back to the bounty.

00:32:51.748 --> 00:32:58.098
Once again, Captain Bly ordered a punishment with the cat and iron tails.

00:32:58.158 --> 00:33:01.322
The other sailors watched the punishment.

00:33:01.382 --> 00:33:06.564
They were sorry for the three men, and they were angry with the captain.

00:33:06.625 --> 00:33:08.276
It's sad.

00:33:08.336 --> 00:33:12.128
One of the sailors said, they're not bad men.

00:33:12.188 --> 00:33:14.740
The captain's too hard.

00:33:14.800 --> 00:33:16.082
You're right.

00:33:16.142 --> 00:33:17.853
Another sailor agreed.

00:33:17.913 --> 00:33:20.322
The captain's a hard man.

00:33:20.382 --> 00:33:25.983
That night, it was very hot, and Tom could not sleep.

00:33:26.043 --> 00:33:28.704
So he walked on the deck.

00:33:28.764 --> 00:33:34.036
He heard a conversation between Fletcher Christian and George.

00:33:34.096 --> 00:33:37.498
You know I'm right, George said.

00:33:37.558 --> 00:33:40.430
It can't continue like this, sir.

00:33:40.490 --> 00:33:42.231
What can we do?

00:33:42.290 --> 00:33:43.971
Fletcher asked.

00:33:44.031 --> 00:33:46.612
You know the answer to that, sir.

00:33:46.673 --> 00:33:48.549
George told him.

00:33:48.609 --> 00:33:51.786
The man are with you, Mr. Christian.

00:33:51.846 --> 00:33:53.817
How many men?

00:33:53.877 --> 00:33:55.668
Fletcher asked him.

00:33:55.728 --> 00:33:57.258
Enough, sir.

00:33:57.318 --> 00:34:00.869
George told him.

00:34:00.929 --> 00:34:07.712
Chapter 8, Tom's big decision.

00:34:07.771 --> 00:34:12.123
The bounty spent six months in Tahiti.

00:34:12.184 --> 00:34:19.348
Finally, the wind was in the right direction, and Captain Bly decided to leave the island.

00:34:19.408 --> 00:34:26.014
The sailors did not want to go back to the ship because they had friends on the island now.

00:34:26.075 --> 00:34:30.838
Some of them even wanted to marry Tahitian girls.

00:34:30.898 --> 00:34:34.610
The ship sailed away from the island.

00:34:34.671 --> 00:34:39.563
The sailors did their work, but they were silent.

00:34:39.624 --> 00:34:42.106
What's wrong with the men?

00:34:42.166 --> 00:34:45.730
Captain Bly asked Fletcher Christian one day.

00:34:45.790 --> 00:34:47.303
They're all right, sir.

00:34:47.363 --> 00:34:48.574
Fletcher told him.

00:34:48.634 --> 00:34:51.326
They just missed their friends on Tahiti.

00:34:51.386 --> 00:34:54.898
Captain Bly turned to Tom with a smile.

00:34:54.958 --> 00:34:57.599
A little navigation, Mr. Barnes?

00:34:57.659 --> 00:34:58.830
He suggested.

00:34:58.890 --> 00:35:01.422
We mustn't forget navigation.

00:35:01.482 --> 00:35:04.103
He gave Tom the Sextant.

00:35:04.164 --> 00:35:06.084
Tom looked at the sun.

00:35:06.144 --> 00:35:09.336
Then he wrote some numbers on a piece of paper.

00:35:09.397 --> 00:35:11.848
He showed the paper to Bly.

00:35:11.908 --> 00:35:14.503
Well done, the captain said.

00:35:14.563 --> 00:35:16.957
You're learning, Mr. Barnes?

00:35:17.017 --> 00:35:21.549
Tom remembered the words of the old sailor at the port.

00:35:21.609 --> 00:35:24.320
Darn everything you can.

00:35:24.380 --> 00:35:27.422
He was very pleased with himself.

00:35:27.482 --> 00:35:31.963
Just then, one of the sailors came onto the deck.

00:35:32.023 --> 00:35:36.685
He stopped in front of Fletcher Christian and said a few words.

00:35:36.745 --> 00:35:39.216
What is it, Mr. Christian?

00:35:39.276 --> 00:35:41.011
Captain Bly asked.

00:35:41.071 --> 00:35:43.256
What does the man want?

00:35:43.316 --> 00:35:45.656
It's the chronometer, sir.

00:35:45.716 --> 00:35:47.197
Fletcher replied.

00:35:47.257 --> 00:35:48.967
It doesn't work.

00:35:49.028 --> 00:35:50.828
Doesn't work?

00:35:50.888 --> 00:35:53.309
Shouted life furiously.

00:35:53.369 --> 00:35:54.049
Why?

00:35:54.109 --> 00:35:55.489
Doesn't it work?

00:35:55.550 --> 00:35:57.520
There's water in it.

00:35:57.580 --> 00:35:58.970
Fletcher told him.

00:35:59.031 --> 00:36:01.341
That's your responsibility.

00:36:01.401 --> 00:36:03.232
Captain Bly told him.

00:36:03.292 --> 00:36:07.206
You're the worst officer on this ship.

00:36:07.266 --> 00:36:13.595
Fletcher did not say anything, but he became red in the face.

00:36:13.655 --> 00:36:17.898
Captain Bligh was angry all that day.

00:36:17.958 --> 00:36:21.992
He did not speak to Fletcher at dinner that evening.

00:36:22.053 --> 00:36:25.385
Tom was sorry for his friend.

00:36:25.445 --> 00:36:32.535
In the middle of the night, when Tom was asleep, a man came into his cabin.

00:36:32.595 --> 00:36:33.760
Wake up!

00:36:33.820 --> 00:36:35.821
The man said quietly.

00:36:35.881 --> 00:36:37.312
Wake up, Tom!

00:36:37.372 --> 00:36:39.684
Tom sat up suddenly.

00:36:39.745 --> 00:36:43.728
He looked around and saw Fletcher in the cabin.

00:36:43.788 --> 00:36:45.148
What is it?

00:36:45.208 --> 00:36:46.480
Is something wrong?

00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:47.720
He asked.

00:36:47.780 --> 00:36:49.442
Listen to me.

00:36:49.502 --> 00:36:52.204
Fletcher said very seriously.

00:36:52.264 --> 00:36:56.528
The sailors don't want to obey Captain Bligh.

00:36:56.588 --> 00:37:00.630
I'm going to be Captain of the Bounty.

00:37:00.690 --> 00:37:02.962
What do you mean?

00:37:03.022 --> 00:37:05.252
Tom asked, shocked.

00:37:05.312 --> 00:37:09.034
We're going to take the ship from Captain Bligh.

00:37:09.094 --> 00:37:10.654
Fletcher told him.

00:37:10.714 --> 00:37:12.555
But that's mutiny.

00:37:12.615 --> 00:37:13.586
Tom said.

00:37:13.646 --> 00:37:15.957
You can't do that, Fletcher.

00:37:16.017 --> 00:37:18.298
Don't argue with me, Tom.

00:37:18.358 --> 00:37:19.578
Fletcher said.

00:37:19.638 --> 00:37:22.149
There isn't much time.

00:37:22.209 --> 00:37:25.500
I just want to ask you one thing.

00:37:25.560 --> 00:37:29.394
Are you with me or with the captain?

00:37:29.455 --> 00:37:31.538
Tom thought hard.

00:37:31.598 --> 00:37:33.850
Fletcher was his friend.

00:37:33.910 --> 00:37:38.192
He was a good man, and he was kind to the sailors.

00:37:38.252 --> 00:37:42.096
But Bly was the captain of the ship.

00:37:42.156 --> 00:37:44.967
Tom did not answer.

00:37:45.027 --> 00:37:46.928
You must tell me.

00:37:46.988 --> 00:37:48.360
Fletcher said.

00:37:48.420 --> 00:37:50.630
You must decide, Tom.

00:37:50.690 --> 00:37:54.694
It's the most important decision of your life.

00:37:54.754 --> 00:37:57.532
Tom looked at his friend.

00:37:57.592 --> 00:38:03.381
Then he remembered his conversation with the old sailor at the port.

00:38:03.441 --> 00:38:06.782
And what's the second thing I must do?

00:38:06.842 --> 00:38:08.712
Tom asked him.

00:38:08.772 --> 00:38:10.293
That's easy.

00:38:10.353 --> 00:38:17.134
The old sailor replied, I'll bay your captain.

00:38:17.194 --> 00:38:21.716
Listening activity.

00:38:21.776 --> 00:38:25.894
I think you're right.

00:38:25.954 --> 00:38:31.102
But it's the wrong thing to do.

00:38:31.162 --> 00:38:38.524
Yes, I understand, but I don't think that's true.

00:38:38.584 --> 00:38:47.226
Well, maybe he's not so bad, but he's not a good leader.

00:38:47.286 --> 00:38:55.320
Yes, you're right, but I don't know about that.

00:38:55.380 --> 00:39:03.664
Oh yes, I don't think it's a good idea either.

00:39:03.725 --> 00:39:17.393
Chapter 9 The Mutiny It was early morning on 28 April 1789.

00:39:17.454 --> 00:39:21.496
Captain Bly was asleep in his cabin.

00:39:21.556 --> 00:39:27.534
Suddenly Fletcher Christian and George came into the cabin.

00:39:27.594 --> 00:39:30.688
They had guns and swords with them.

00:39:30.748 --> 00:39:32.158
What is it?

00:39:32.218 --> 00:39:33.889
Shouted Captain Bligh.

00:39:33.949 --> 00:39:35.210
What's wrong?

00:39:35.270 --> 00:39:37.240
This is a mutiny.

00:39:37.300 --> 00:39:40.942
Fletcher told him, I'm the captain now.

00:39:41.002 --> 00:39:43.633
How can you do this, Mr. Christian?

00:39:43.693 --> 00:39:46.274
Captain Bligh asked in great surprise.

00:39:46.334 --> 00:39:48.784
We're officers in the Navy.

00:39:48.844 --> 00:39:51.186
It's too late, Captain Bligh.

00:39:51.246 --> 00:39:55.787
Christian replied, I can't stand your cruelty anymore.

00:39:55.847 --> 00:39:57.944
And neither can the men.

00:39:58.004 --> 00:40:02.634
Christian and George tied the captain's hands behind his back.

00:40:02.694 --> 00:40:05.126
Then they took him onto the deck.

00:40:05.186 --> 00:40:10.029
There were other sailors there, and they had guns and swords as well.

00:40:10.089 --> 00:40:12.831
What can we do with Captain Bligh?

00:40:12.891 --> 00:40:14.412
A sailor asked.

00:40:14.472 --> 00:40:16.263
We can kill him.

00:40:16.323 --> 00:40:18.224
George said.

00:40:18.284 --> 00:40:22.998
I have a wife and four children at home, Mr. Christian.

00:40:23.058 --> 00:40:25.590
Captain Bligh said quietly.

00:40:25.650 --> 00:40:28.133
Are you going to kill me?

00:40:28.193 --> 00:40:29.435
No.

00:40:29.495 --> 00:40:31.016
Fletcher replied.

00:40:31.076 --> 00:40:33.466
I don't want to kill you, Captain.

00:40:33.526 --> 00:40:35.547
He thought for a moment.

00:40:35.607 --> 00:40:38.708
We can give you one of the ship's boats.

00:40:38.768 --> 00:40:40.319
He decided.

00:40:40.379 --> 00:40:42.750
George laughed.

00:40:42.810 --> 00:40:45.210
We're in the middle of the sea.

00:40:45.270 --> 00:40:46.131
He said.

00:40:46.191 --> 00:40:49.792
No one can survive in a small boat.

00:40:49.852 --> 00:40:52.203
It's too dangerous.

00:40:52.263 --> 00:40:56.489
He looked at Captain Bly and smiled cruelly.

00:40:56.549 --> 00:41:00.266
You're going to die out there, Captain.

00:41:00.326 --> 00:41:01.586
He told him.

00:41:01.647 --> 00:41:06.760
You're going to die out there, all alone.

00:41:06.821 --> 00:41:09.442
What do you want to do?

00:41:09.502 --> 00:41:12.214
Fletcher Christian asked the sailors.

00:41:12.274 --> 00:41:17.518
How many of you want to go with Captain Bligh in the small boat?

00:41:17.578 --> 00:41:20.790
Eighteen sailors came forward.

00:41:20.850 --> 00:41:22.620
We do so.

00:41:22.680 --> 00:41:24.432
They told Captain Bligh.

00:41:24.492 --> 00:41:26.666
We're not music ears.

00:41:26.726 --> 00:41:30.550
Tom looked at Fletcher Christian and the mutineers.

00:41:30.610 --> 00:41:33.212
Then he looked at Captain Bly.

00:41:33.272 --> 00:41:35.302
He thought for a moment.

00:41:35.362 --> 00:41:37.834
Then he stepped forward.

00:41:37.894 --> 00:41:40.685
I'm going with the Captain too.

00:41:40.745 --> 00:41:43.326
He told Fletcher Christian.

00:41:43.386 --> 00:41:44.617
You?

00:41:44.677 --> 00:41:45.888
Said Christian.

00:41:45.948 --> 00:41:48.138
But it's dangerous, Tom.

00:41:48.198 --> 00:41:49.810
Stay with us.

00:41:49.870 --> 00:41:52.040
You're my friend.

00:41:52.100 --> 00:41:53.891
No Fletcher.

00:41:53.951 --> 00:41:55.252
Tom replied.

00:41:55.312 --> 00:41:57.952
I must obey my captain.

00:41:58.012 --> 00:42:01.184
Soon the small boat was ready to leave.

00:42:01.244 --> 00:42:05.746
Captain Bligh, Tom, and the eighteen sailors got into it.

00:42:05.806 --> 00:42:12.619
They had a little water and food with them, and Captain Bligh carried his sextant with him.

00:42:12.679 --> 00:42:16.171
Captain Bligh sat at the back of the boat.

00:42:16.231 --> 00:42:18.932
He looked at Tom and the sailors.

00:42:18.992 --> 00:42:22.603
He was serious, but very calm.

00:42:22.664 --> 00:42:24.786
Raise the sail.

00:42:24.846 --> 00:42:30.230
He told the sailors, the boat sailed away from the bounty.

00:42:30.290 --> 00:42:32.491
And now Mr. Barnes?

00:42:32.551 --> 00:42:37.462
Captain Bly said with a smile, some navigation.

00:42:37.522 --> 00:42:41.934
Bly took out his sextant and looked at the sun.

00:42:41.994 --> 00:42:45.276
Then he made some calculations.

00:42:45.336 --> 00:42:47.586
We're a long way from land.

00:42:47.646 --> 00:42:49.607
He told the men in the boat.

00:42:49.667 --> 00:42:52.601
We don't have much food or water.

00:42:52.662 --> 00:42:55.206
But we can survive.

00:42:55.266 --> 00:42:58.608
I promise you, we can survive.

00:42:58.668 --> 00:43:00.540
Discipline, men.

00:43:00.600 --> 00:43:02.042
Discipline.

00:43:02.102 --> 00:43:06.314
Captain Bligh took the boat to some small islands.

00:43:06.374 --> 00:43:10.018
They bought some food and water from the people there.

00:43:10.078 --> 00:43:15.582
After that, they were ready to begin their journey.

00:43:15.642 --> 00:43:28.296
Chapter 10 Land It was hot on the small boat, and there was no protection from the sun.

00:43:28.357 --> 00:43:32.670
After a week, the men were hungry and thirsty.

00:43:32.730 --> 00:43:36.893
Captain Bly used his sextant every day.

00:43:36.954 --> 00:43:40.486
He tried to make his men feel better.

00:43:40.547 --> 00:43:42.168
We're sailors.

00:43:42.228 --> 00:43:43.259
He told them.

00:43:43.319 --> 00:43:49.492
We can survive hunger and thirst, and we have the discipline for this voyage.

00:43:49.552 --> 00:43:53.532
Captain Bly told the sailors that he had a plan.

00:43:53.592 --> 00:43:56.986
We'll go to the island of Tafoa, he said.

00:43:57.046 --> 00:44:00.087
We can buy more food and water there.

00:44:00.148 --> 00:44:02.930
The men believed in their captain.

00:44:02.990 --> 00:44:07.904
He was always calm and he always knew where the boat was.

00:44:07.964 --> 00:44:10.976
He was not afraid of the sea.

00:44:11.036 --> 00:44:15.182
They soon arrived at the island of Tafoa.

00:44:15.242 --> 00:44:21.497
At first, the islanders were friendly and they brought the sailors food and drink.

00:44:21.557 --> 00:44:24.598
But soon they began to change.

00:44:24.658 --> 00:44:28.509
They attacked the sailors and killed one of them.

00:44:28.569 --> 00:44:33.450
Captain Bligh gave the order to sail away from the island.

00:44:33.510 --> 00:44:39.082
Now they only had enough food and water for five days.

00:44:39.142 --> 00:44:41.202
Listen to me, man.

00:44:41.263 --> 00:44:50.514
Captain Bligh said, We must sail to Koopang, but the journey will take 50 days.

00:44:50.574 --> 00:44:55.296
We must eat and drink very little.

00:44:55.357 --> 00:45:01.110
It will be difficult and dangerous, but we can do it.

00:45:01.170 --> 00:45:03.201
What do you say?

00:45:03.262 --> 00:45:05.652
Will you follow my orders?

00:45:05.712 --> 00:45:10.485
The sailors agreed to follow their captain's orders.

00:45:10.545 --> 00:45:13.776
The sea was full of sharks.

00:45:13.837 --> 00:45:15.908
They followed the boat.

00:45:15.968 --> 00:45:18.751
Don't put your hands in the water.

00:45:18.811 --> 00:45:21.382
Captain Bligh told the sailors.

00:45:21.442 --> 00:45:24.806
The sharks are hungry too.

00:45:24.866 --> 00:45:28.008
The sea was flat and calm.

00:45:28.069 --> 00:45:30.950
The boat sailed through the waves.

00:45:31.010 --> 00:45:36.636
Suddenly the sea became rough and the boat moved from side to side.

00:45:36.696 --> 00:45:38.727
Tom was afraid.

00:45:38.787 --> 00:45:40.437
It's a whale!"

00:45:40.497 --> 00:45:42.778
One of the sailors cried.

00:45:42.838 --> 00:45:47.548
Then Tom saw an enormous whale come out of the sea.

00:45:47.609 --> 00:45:50.589
The whale was larger than their boat.

00:45:50.649 --> 00:45:52.949
Captain Bligh laughed.

00:45:53.010 --> 00:45:55.330
Ah, don't be frightened, Mr. Barnes.

00:45:55.390 --> 00:45:56.970
He said kindly.

00:45:57.030 --> 00:45:59.581
Whales don't attack boats.

00:45:59.641 --> 00:46:01.851
The weather quickly changed.

00:46:01.911 --> 00:46:06.650
The sky was full of clouds, and there was a strong wind.

00:46:06.710 --> 00:46:09.389
A storm is coming, sir.

00:46:09.449 --> 00:46:12.530
One of the sailors said to Captain Bligh.

00:46:12.590 --> 00:46:15.751
Captain Bligh saw that he was right.

00:46:15.811 --> 00:46:17.632
Take the sail down, men.

00:46:17.692 --> 00:46:19.632
He commanded.

00:46:19.692 --> 00:46:22.643
Soon the storm arrived.

00:46:22.704 --> 00:46:26.925
The waves were very big and the boat was full of water.

00:46:26.985 --> 00:46:32.437
The storm lasted all that day and continued all that night.

00:46:32.497 --> 00:46:36.182
The sailors were wet and tired.

00:46:36.243 --> 00:46:41.284
It was now the 30th day of their voyage in the boat.

00:46:41.344 --> 00:46:43.768
The men were exhausted.

00:46:43.828 --> 00:46:49.949
They wanted to rest, but they continued to obey Captain Bligh's orders.

00:46:50.010 --> 00:46:53.494
Suddenly, one of the sailors looked up.

00:46:53.554 --> 00:46:54.894
A sail!

00:46:54.954 --> 00:46:55.974
He shouted.

00:46:56.034 --> 00:46:58.466
There's a ship over there, Sir!

00:46:58.526 --> 00:47:00.066
It was true.

00:47:00.126 --> 00:47:02.798
They saw a sail in the distance.

00:47:02.858 --> 00:47:04.778
They started to shout.

00:47:04.838 --> 00:47:07.200
They wanted the ship to see them.

00:47:07.260 --> 00:47:12.622
They shouted for a long time, but the ship did not see their boat.

00:47:12.682 --> 00:47:16.784
After a while, they could not see the sail anymore.

00:47:16.844 --> 00:47:19.198
The men were sad now.

00:47:19.259 --> 00:47:21.412
They had no hope.

00:47:21.473 --> 00:47:25.744
We're going to die, one of them said.

00:47:25.804 --> 00:47:28.955
My sextant, please, Mr. Barnes.

00:47:29.015 --> 00:47:31.216
Captain Bly said to Tom.

00:47:31.276 --> 00:47:34.137
I must discover where we are.

00:47:34.197 --> 00:47:40.659
Captain Bly looked through the sextant and wrote some numbers on a piece of paper.

00:47:40.720 --> 00:47:42.470
Good news, men.

00:47:42.530 --> 00:47:44.160
He told the sailors.

00:47:44.220 --> 00:47:46.101
We're near land.

00:47:46.162 --> 00:47:48.463
How many days, sir?

00:47:48.523 --> 00:47:51.024
One of the sailors wanted to know.

00:47:51.084 --> 00:47:52.586
Ten days?

00:47:52.646 --> 00:47:53.986
Two weeks?

00:47:54.046 --> 00:47:56.138
Captain Bly told him.

00:47:56.198 --> 00:48:01.682
And then food and water, as much as we want.

00:48:01.742 --> 00:48:05.564
The sailors looked at their captain with respect.

00:48:05.624 --> 00:48:07.825
They trusted him now.

00:48:07.885 --> 00:48:10.356
He was a good navigator.

00:48:10.417 --> 00:48:13.356
They started to hope again.

00:48:13.416 --> 00:48:18.298
It was the 47th day at sea in the boat.

00:48:18.358 --> 00:48:21.260
The men had no strength.

00:48:21.321 --> 00:48:25.714
It was difficult for them to raise and lower the sail.

00:48:25.774 --> 00:48:28.796
They needed food and water.

00:48:28.856 --> 00:48:33.748
It was a hot day, and some of the sailors were asleep.

00:48:33.808 --> 00:48:36.801
Captain Bly talked to Tom.

00:48:36.861 --> 00:48:39.363
They're good men, he said.

00:48:39.423 --> 00:48:42.880
They have discipline, Mr. Barnes.

00:48:42.940 --> 00:48:49.983
The Navy needs discipline, discipline, and good navigation.

00:48:50.043 --> 00:48:57.340
On the 12th of June, 1789, one of the sailors gave a shout.

00:48:57.400 --> 00:48:59.132
Lancer!

00:48:59.192 --> 00:49:01.916
I can see land over there!

00:49:01.976 --> 00:49:04.288
The other sailors woke up.

00:49:04.348 --> 00:49:06.526
They looked out of the boat.

00:49:06.586 --> 00:49:08.082
It's true!

00:49:08.142 --> 00:49:08.993
They cried.

00:49:09.053 --> 00:49:10.273
Lancer!

00:49:10.333 --> 00:49:11.453
Land!

00:49:11.513 --> 00:49:14.544
Captain Bly smiled at them.

00:49:14.604 --> 00:49:17.435
It is land, indeed.

00:49:17.495 --> 00:49:18.966
He told them.

00:49:19.026 --> 00:49:21.966
This is Timor.

00:49:22.026 --> 00:49:24.527
Soon they were on land.

00:49:24.587 --> 00:49:31.839
Their journey of 7,000 kilometers was over.

00:49:31.899 --> 00:49:35.850
Epilogue.

00:49:35.910 --> 00:49:38.960
Tom returned to England.

00:49:39.020 --> 00:49:43.974
He became a good officer and was popular with the sailors.

00:49:44.034 --> 00:49:53.078
Two years after the mutiny, another British ship, HMS Pandora, arrived in Tahiti.

00:49:53.138 --> 00:49:58.802
The sailors from HMS Pandora looked for the mutineers from the bounty.

00:49:58.862 --> 00:50:03.986
They found 14 sailors and took them back to England.

00:50:04.046 --> 00:50:11.610
But during the journey the ship hit a rock near Australia and some of the mutineers died.

00:50:11.670 --> 00:50:15.050
Other ships took them back to England.

00:50:15.110 --> 00:50:18.741
When they arrived there was a trial.

00:50:18.802 --> 00:50:22.842
Mutiny was a very serious crime.

00:50:22.902 --> 00:50:31.694
Three mutineers received the death penalty, but the judges decided that the others were innocent.

00:50:31.754 --> 00:50:34.483
The years passed.

00:50:34.543 --> 00:50:39.764
Tom became a successful captain and commanded his own ship.

00:50:39.824 --> 00:50:47.398
He wanted to know about Fletcher Christian and the bounty, but there was no information.

00:50:47.458 --> 00:51:00.490
Then, in 1808, nineteen years after the mutiny, an American ship came to the small island of Pitcairn in the Pacific.

00:51:00.550 --> 00:51:05.658
Captain Folger discovered a white man on the island.

00:51:05.718 --> 00:51:12.922
He was a sailor called Adams, the only survivor of the bounty mutineers.

00:51:12.982 --> 00:51:17.374
Now he was old and he had a family.

00:51:17.435 --> 00:51:21.947
Adams told Captain Folger the story of the bounty.

00:51:22.008 --> 00:51:26.020
We took the bounty back to Taiiti after the mutiny.

00:51:26.080 --> 00:51:27.292
He explained.

00:51:27.352 --> 00:51:34.845
Some Polynesian men and Tahitian women came with us and we sailed here to Pitcan.

00:51:34.905 --> 00:51:37.476
We burned the bounty.

00:51:37.536 --> 00:51:43.577
We didn't want people to find it because we were afraid of punishment.

00:51:43.637 --> 00:51:46.138
What happened then?

00:51:46.198 --> 00:51:48.768
Captain Folger wanted to know.

00:51:48.828 --> 00:51:50.749
It was terrible.

00:51:50.809 --> 00:51:52.069
Adam said.

00:51:52.129 --> 00:51:56.746
We argued with the Polynesian men all the time.

00:51:56.806 --> 00:52:02.455
We fought a battle against them, and Fletcher Christian died.

00:52:02.515 --> 00:52:09.808
Some of the mutineers died in the battle as well, and we killed all the Polynesian men.

00:52:09.868 --> 00:52:12.148
But you're the only survivor.

00:52:12.208 --> 00:52:16.950
Captain Folger exclaimed, what happened after the battle?

00:52:17.010 --> 00:52:19.981
It was the Tahitian women.

00:52:20.041 --> 00:52:21.762
Adams explained.

00:52:21.822 --> 00:52:26.655
They weren't happy with us, and they killed most of us.

00:52:26.715 --> 00:52:29.438
The rest died of illness.

00:52:29.498 --> 00:52:34.332
Captain Folger brought the news about the bounty to England.

00:52:34.392 --> 00:52:41.768
Now Tom finally knew the truth about his friend Fletcher Christian and the other mutineers.

00:52:41.828 --> 00:52:47.952
He was sad when he thought about his friend from the early days of his career.

00:52:48.012 --> 00:52:53.681
Then he remembered again the words of the old sailor at the port.

00:52:53.742 --> 00:52:57.850
That's one of the two things you must do.

00:52:57.910 --> 00:53:01.682
Learn everything you can.

00:53:01.743 --> 00:53:04.825
And what's the second thing I must do?

00:53:04.885 --> 00:53:06.216
That's easy.

00:53:06.276 --> 00:53:08.568
The old sailor replied.

00:53:08.628 --> 00:53:12.190
Obey your captain.

00:53:12.250 --> 00:53:14.361
It was good advice.

00:53:14.421 --> 00:53:15.882
Thought Tom.

00:53:15.942 --> 00:53:22.891
Fletcher made a bad mistake when he mutinied against Captain Bly.

00:53:22.951 --> 00:53:27.748
Listening activity.

00:53:27.808 --> 00:53:30.500
What is your name?

00:53:30.560 --> 00:53:33.131
My name is John Fletcher.

00:53:33.191 --> 00:53:35.142
How old are you?

00:53:35.162 --> 00:53:37.444
18.

00:53:37.504 --> 00:53:39.884
Where were you born?

00:53:39.944 --> 00:53:41.686
Newcastle.

00:53:41.746 --> 00:53:43.957
Where do you live now?

00:53:44.017 --> 00:53:45.728
London.

00:53:45.788 --> 00:53:48.079
Are you still a sailor?

00:53:48.139 --> 00:53:49.360
No.

00:53:49.420 --> 00:53:53.924
I can't work in the Navy because I'm here on trial.

00:53:53.984 --> 00:53:57.238
I now work as a carpenter.

00:53:57.298 --> 00:54:00.630
What was your road and the mutiny?

00:54:00.690 --> 00:54:09.146
I didn't want to take part in the mutiny, but there was no more room in the small boat to go with the captain.

00:54:09.206 --> 00:54:15.170
I returned to England when they came to find us on the island of Tahiti.

